1
00:00:02,850 --> 00:00:05,505
Cal Hacks. Hundreds of people in one hangar,

2
00:00:05,505 --> 00:00:08,097
and any one of them could change what you build.

3
00:00:08,117 --> 00:00:11,563
Meeting people in person is still how teams and ideas start.

4
00:00:11,583 --> 00:00:15,463
But while you talk to one person, you can't talk to anyone else.

5
00:00:15,483 --> 00:00:17,440
So every hello is a gamble. In one study,

6
00:00:17,440 --> 00:00:20,944
ninety five percent of guests wanted to meet new people,

7
00:00:20,944 --> 00:00:24,263
yet half their conversations were with friends they already knew.

8
00:00:24,283 --> 00:00:25,930
What if the room had a filter?

9
00:00:25,950 --> 00:00:29,398
Meet the Human Human Interaction Lab. Your phone, on a lanyard,

10
00:00:29,398 --> 00:00:31,163
becomes a live name badge.

11
00:00:31,183 --> 00:00:32,378
You onboard by text.

12
00:00:32,378 --> 00:00:35,547
Our iMessage agent asks who you are and who you want to meet,

13
00:00:35,547 --> 00:00:37,730
then sends you its contact card.

14
00:00:37,750 --> 00:00:39,620
Your badge shows your name, huge,

15
00:00:39,620 --> 00:00:42,097
plus the topics people should ask you about.

16
00:00:42,117 --> 00:00:42,926
Behind the scenes,

17
00:00:42,926 --> 00:00:45,410
every pair of attendees is scored in both directions.

18
00:00:45,410 --> 00:00:47,463
Only mutual matches light up.

19
00:00:47,483 --> 00:00:50,451
Wear the badge and walk the room. As a match gets closer,

20
00:00:50,451 --> 00:00:51,959
measured by Ultra Wideband,

21
00:00:51,959 --> 00:00:54,186
both badges tint toward a shared color,

22
00:00:54,186 --> 00:00:57,230
and the topics flip to what they want to talk to you about.

23
00:00:57,250 --> 00:00:59,153
Within two meters, the avatars jump together,

24
00:00:59,153 --> 00:01:01,997
and the conversation starts recording, with consent.

25
00:01:02,017 --> 00:01:02,913
When you part ways,

26
00:01:02,913 --> 00:01:05,763
you get a summary and a follow up you can send.

27
00:01:05,783 --> 00:01:08,063
And everyone you met lives in your People list.

28
00:01:08,083 --> 00:01:08,795
Under the hood,

29
00:01:08,795 --> 00:01:12,010
the iPhone ranges nearby badges and syncs live to Convex,

30
00:01:12,010 --> 00:01:14,317
with SpacetimeDB as a second backend.

31
00:01:14,317 --> 00:01:17,163
Photon carries the conversation over iMessage.

32
00:01:17,183 --> 00:01:20,005
TypeSafe's Jev rates every pair in half a second,

33
00:01:20,005 --> 00:01:21,753
Claude writes why you should meet,

34
00:01:21,753 --> 00:01:25,463
and a geometric mean makes one sided interest score low.

35
00:01:25,483 --> 00:01:29,730
Every screen, avatar and sound was designed in Figma first.

36
00:01:29,750 --> 00:01:33,650
Human Human Interaction Lab. Fewer gambles, better hellos.
